
  <section class="page-hero">
    <div class="container">
      <p class="eyebrow">Ways to give</p>
      <h1>Every dollar stays in Flagler County.</h1>
      <p>We are a 501(c)(3), EIN 27-1349987. Your contribution is tax deductible.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Donation form -->
  <section class="section" id="donate">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="hero__grid">
        <div>
          <p class="eyebrow">Give online</p>
          <h2>Make a gift now.</h2>
          <p>
            Choose a one-time gift or a monthly one. Monthly is more useful to us than the same
            money given once — it is what lets us say yes to a request in the middle of the year.
          </p>

          <div class="callout callout--gold">
            <h3>Why our donation form has no platform fee</h3>
            <p class="mb-0">
              We use <strong>Zeffy</strong>, which charges nonprofits nothing — no platform fee
              and no card processing fee. Zeffy funds itself with an optional tip that donors can
              adjust or decline at checkout. If you would rather all of your gift reach the
              Foundation, set the tip to zero; nothing is deducted from your donation either way.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div data-donate-setup>
            <div class="placeholder mt-5">
              <p><strong>[SETUP — FOUNDATION ACTION REQUIRED]</strong> The donation form is not
              connected yet. To switch it on:</p>
              <ol>
                <li>Create the account at <a href="https://www.zeffy.com" rel="noopener">zeffy.com</a> using EIN 27-1349987.</li>
                <li>Build one donation form and enable the monthly option.</li>
                <li>Copy the form's share URL and paste the slug into <code>js/donate-config.js</code>.</li>
              </ol>
              <p class="mb-0">The form embeds itself here automatically once that slug is set.
              Until then, the PayPal button and the mail-in option below both work.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div>
          <div class="donate-embed" id="donate-embed">
            <div style="padding:2rem">
              <h3>Give today</h3>
              <p>Our no-fee donation form appears here once it is connected.</p>
              <p><strong>In the meantime, both of these work right now:</strong></p>
              <p>
                <a class="btn btn--donate btn--block btn--lg" href="https://www.paypal.com/donate?hosted_button_id=Z4S96Q5ZEGJE4" rel="noopener">Donate with PayPal</a>
              </p>
              <p class="field__help">Or mail a check — details below. PayPal deducts a
              processing fee; mailing a check and the Zeffy form do not.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Monthly -->
  <section class="section section--tint" id="monthly">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section__head">
        <p class="eyebrow">Club 100</p>
        <h2>$10 a month. A hundred neighbors. A year of steady support.</h2>
        <p class="lede">
          Club 100 is our monthly giving circle — $120 a year, or $10 a month. It is the most
          useful money the Foundation receives, because it arrives whether or not there is a
          grant, an event, or a good news cycle.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="grid grid--3">
        <div class="tier">
          <p class="tier__amount">$10<span style="font-size:1rem;font-weight:400">/mo</span></p>
          <p class="tier__buys">Club 100 member</p>
          <p>$120 over a year. Your name joins the Club 100 list, and you are thanked at the
          annual Ride for Recovery.</p>
          <a class="btn btn--outline" href="#donate" data-donate data-amount="10" data-monthly="true">Join Club 100</a>
        </div>

        <div class="tier tier--featured">
          <span class="tier__flag">Most useful</span>
          <p class="tier__amount">$25<span style="font-size:1rem;font-weight:400">/mo</span></p>
          <p class="tier__buys">Sustaining supporter</p>
          <p>Enough to keep one participant supplied with the practical supports that keep them
          in the program — consistently, all year.</p>
          <a class="btn btn--primary" href="#donate" data-donate data-amount="25" data-monthly="true">Give $25 a month</a>
        </div>

        <div class="tier">
          <p class="tier__amount">$50<span style="font-size:1rem;font-weight:400">/mo</span></p>
          <p class="tier__buys">Founding circle</p>
          <p>Underwrites a meaningful share of a year's Narcan supply and graduation costs.</p>
          <a class="btn btn--outline" href="#donate" data-donate data-amount="50" data-monthly="true">Give $50 a month</a>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="placeholder mt-6 narrow">
        <p class="mb-0"><strong>[CLIENT TO CONFIRM]</strong> The $10 Club 100 tier is real and
        carried over from your existing materials. The $25 and $50 descriptions are structural
        placeholders — tell us what those amounts actually cover and we will make the wording
        literal instead of approximate.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- One-time / designated -->
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section__head">
        <p class="eyebrow">One-time gifts</p>
        <h2>Give toward something specific.</h2>
      </div>

      <div class="grid grid--3">
        <div class="tier">
          <p class="tier__amount">$<span data-cost-placeholder>&nbsp;&mdash;&nbsp;</span></p>
          <p class="tier__buys">Narcan kits</p>
          <p>Free two-dose naloxone kits for families, community events, and people leaving
          treatment.</p>
          <a class="btn btn--outline" href="#donate" data-donate data-amount="">Give this</a>
        </div>
        <div class="tier">
          <p class="tier__amount">$<span data-cost-placeholder>&nbsp;&mdash;&nbsp;</span></p>
          <p class="tier__buys">A ride to treatment</p>
          <p>Transportation to treatment and court appearances — one of the most common reasons
          someone cannot continue.</p>
          <a class="btn btn--outline" href="#donate" data-donate data-amount="">Give this</a>
        </div>
        <div class="tier">
          <p class="tier__amount">$<span data-cost-placeholder>&nbsp;&mdash;&nbsp;</span></p>
          <p class="tier__buys">Testing &amp; graduation</p>
          <p>Drug testing that makes accountability real, and graduation costs that make
          finishing feel like an achievement.</p>
          <a class="btn btn--outline" href="#donate" data-donate data-amount="">Give this</a>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="placeholder mt-6 narrow">
        <p class="mb-0"><strong>[CLIENT MUST SUPPLY REAL COSTS]</strong> These amounts are blank
        on purpose — we will not guess at what your programme actually spends. Send the real
        per-item costs and we will fill all three in (they are set once, in
        <code>ways-to-give.html</code> and <code>index.html</code>).</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Business sponsorship -->
  <section class="section section--warm" id="business">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="hero__grid">
        <div>
          <p class="eyebrow">Local businesses</p>
          <h2>Sponsor the Foundation.</h2>
          <p>
            Business sponsors are listed on this site, recognised at the annual Ride for
            Recovery, and thanked in our community materials. For a local business, this is
            visible support for a program that reduces crime and returns employable neighbors
            to the workforce.
          </p>
          <p>
            We are glad to put together a sponsorship letter for your accountant, and we can
            provide our determination letter and W-9 on request.
          </p>
          <div class="btn-row mt-5">
            <a class="btn btn--primary" href="contact.html?subject=sponsor">Talk to us about sponsoring</a>
          </div>

          <div class="placeholder mt-6">
            <p class="mb-0"><strong>[CLIENT TO SUPPLY]</strong> If you have set sponsorship
            levels (e.g. Bronze/Silver/Gold, or Ride for Recovery event tiers) with prices and
            benefits, send them and we will publish a proper sponsorship table here.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div>
          <div class="card">
            <h3>Current supporters</h3>
            <p>Businesses and neighbors already giving.</p>
            <div class="logo-wall" style="grid-template-columns:repeat(2,1fr)">
              <img src="assets/img/sponsor-MinuteManPress.webp" alt="Minuteman Press" loading="lazy" width="400" height="122">
              <img src="assets/img/sponsor-TravelLeaders.webp" alt="Travel Leaders" loading="lazy" width="400" height="145">
              <img src="assets/img/sponsor-EaglePest-2.webp" alt="Eagle Pest Solutions" loading="lazy" width="400" height="107">
              <img src="assets/img/sponsor-JobOne.webp" alt="Alan Lowe LLC" loading="lazy" width="400" height="167">
              <img src="assets/img/sponsor-GoodVibes.webp" alt="Good Vibe Energy &amp; Nutrition" loading="lazy" width="400" height="217">
              <img src="assets/img/sponsor-Coastal-church2.webp" alt="Coastal Family Church" loading="lazy" width="400" height="219">
              <img src="assets/img/sponsor-CutUpSew.webp" alt="Cut Up &amp; Sew" loading="lazy" width="400" height="265">
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Other ways -->
  <section class="section" id="mail">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section__head">
        <p class="eyebrow">Other ways to give</p>
        <h2>By mail, by event, by hand.</h2>
      </div>

      <div class="grid grid--3">
        <div class="card">
          <div class="card__icon">
            <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="2" y="5" width="20" height="14" rx="2"/><path d="m2 7 10 6 10-6"/></svg>
          </div>
          <h3>Give by mail</h3>
          <p>
            Checks payable to <strong>The Flagler County Drug Court Foundation</strong>.
            No processing fees are deducted from a mailed gift.
          </p>
          <p class="mb-0">
            <strong>55 Black Alder Dr<br>Palm Coast, FL 32137</strong>
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="card">
          <div class="card__icon">
            <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M3 12h4l2-5 3 10 2-5h7"/></svg>
          </div>
          <h3>Ride for Recovery</h3>
          <p>
            Our annual fundraiser — a ride open to all vehicles, with a pig roast, raffle,
            auction, and vendor fair. Riders, vendors and sponsors all welcome.
          </p>
          <a class="btn btn--outline" href="contact.html?subject=ride">Ask about the next ride</a>
        </div>

        <div class="card">
          <div class="card__icon">
            <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M16 21v-2a4 4 0 0 0-4-4H6a4 4 0 0 0-4 4v2"/><circle cx="9" cy="7" r="4"/><path d="M22 21v-2a4 4 0 0 0-3-3.9"/></svg>
          </div>
          <h3>Give time</h3>
          <p>
            Volunteers staff events, hand out Narcan, and help at the annual ride. If you have
            a skill and a few hours, we will find a use for both.
          </p>
          <a class="btn btn--outline" href="contact.html?subject=volunteer">Volunteer</a>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="callout mt-6 narrow">
        <h3>Tax receipts and paperwork</h3>
        <p class="mb-0">
          The Flagler County Drug Court Foundation is a recognised 501(c)(3) organisation and
          all financial contributions are tax deductible to the extent allowed by law. Our EIN
          is <strong>27-1349987</strong>. Need a receipt, our determination letter, or a W-9?
          <a href="contact.html">Ask us</a>.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
